    "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nThis PR addresses a PostgreSQL-specific failure in the `/grim history` command path by changing how UUID values are read from JDBC `ResultSet`s, aiming to support drivers that return native `UUID` objects rather than 16-byte arrays.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Updated `Violation.fromResultSet()` to use a new UUID extraction helper instead of assuming UUID columns are `byte[]`.\n- Added `DatabaseUtils.getUuid(ResultSet, String)` to support reading UUIDs as either `UUID` or `byte[]`.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 2 out of 2 changed files in this pull request and generated 2 comments.\n\n| File | Description |\n| ---- | ----------- |\n| `common/src/main/java/ac/grim/grimac/manager/violationdatabase/Violation.java` | Switches UUID retrieval to the new `DatabaseUtils.getUuid(...)` helper. |\n| `common/src/main/java/ac/grim/grimac/manager/violationdatabase/DatabaseUtils.java` | Introduces a helper to decode UUID values from `ResultSet` across DB backends/drivers. |\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/GrimAnticheat/Grim/new/2.0?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
